{
  "id": "ticket_01KY93E2BKH5JCMAV3JWPNN63G",
  "name": "update/draft/undraft: lock-free read-modify-write can silently revert concurrent transitions",
  "slug": "update-draft-undraft-lock-free-read-modify-write-can-silentl",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "update, draft, and undraft mutate without withLock and write a stale expectedAfter, silently reverting a concurrent start/done/stop — resurrecting terminal tickets and orphaning live sessions.",
    "details_md": "They are the ONLY three mutating commands without withLock (new/split/edit/start/stop/done/drop/review/plan all lock and re-read inside). runUpdate reads the ticket outside any lock, computes the target from that stale snapshot, and updateTicket writes it; on any mismatch the JSONC layer falls back to writeCanonical(expectedAfter), overwriting a concurrent committed change. Reachable with no --state and no hand-edit, on the parallel-agent scenario v0 targets.",
    "acceptance": [
      "runUpdate, runDraft, runUndraft each acquire withLock(paths.lockFile) and RE-READ the ticket by resolved id inside the lock before buildUpdate and updateTicket",
      "A regression test spawns two concurrent processes (update vs start, and update vs done) and asserts neither committed transition is reverted and no session is orphaned"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/cli/commands/update.ts:17-46 (no withLock; reads at :23, writes at :39)",
      "src/cli/commands/draft.ts:13-38 and undraft.ts:13-39 (same pattern)",
      "src/core/jsonc.ts:199-209 (writeCanonical(expectedAfter) fallback)",
      "src/repo/tickets.ts:74 updateTicket (no internal lock)"
    ],
    "meta": {},
    "v": 1
  },
  "state": "done",
